#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065375 :tutorial/content "To multiply a binomial and a trinomial, we take each term of the binomial and multiply it by every term in the trinomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\nFor example, to multiply $({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})$ and $(x^2 + 2x+4),$ we multiply ${\\color{blue}{x}}$ and $(x^2 + 2x+4),$ and then we add this to the product of ${\\color{red}{3}}$ and $(x^2 + 2x+4).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)({x}^{2}+2x+4) & = \\\\ x({x}^{2}+2x+4)+3({x}^{2}+2x+4) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4x+3{x}^{2}+6x+12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we group the like terms and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4x+3{x}^{2}+6x+12 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+3{x}^{2}+4x+6x+12 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+10x+12\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "abdf5593-94a7-5f4c-a2ec-ca378d5b0034" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4089 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
